%erg 0.1
Title: Refactor docs-build workflow to always-run with internal chore-filter
Created: 2026-05-28
Author: HDMX-coding-agent

--- log ---
2026-05-28T13:30Z HDMX-coding-agent created — surfaced by 0358 raid: GitHub branch protection requires the `build` status to report on every PR, but the current `pull_request.paths` trigger skips PRs that don't touch build inputs (STATE.md, ticket-only PRs, .claude/** edits). Required-check + skipped workflow = unmergeable PR.

--- body ---
## Context

The `docs-build` workflow added by ticket 0365 uses `pull_request.paths` to
trigger only on PRs touching `report/**`, `slides/**`, `Makefile`,
`experiments/analysis.mk`, `src/aedist/**`, `tests/**`, `data/**`, or
`.github/workflows/docs-build.yml`. That's the right scope for *running*
the build, but it has a fatal interaction with branch protection:

> A required status check that never reports on a PR keeps the PR pending
> forever — the merge button stays disabled.

Ticket 0358 needs to add `build` (the docs-build job) to the required
status checks on `main`. PR #638 (0358's deliverable) only edits STATE.md;
under the current trigger it does not start `docs-build`. Required-check
+ workflow-never-runs = PR #638 cannot merge. The same trap waits for
every future STATE/ticket-only PR.

## Fix

Mirror the pattern already used by `.github/workflows/CI.yml`:

1. Remove `pull_request.paths` from `docs-build.yml`'s trigger so the
   workflow starts on every PR.
2. Add a `changes` job (or reuse its `predicate-quantifier: every` filter
   pattern) that detects chore-only diffs (`tickets/**`, `STATE.md`,
   `.claude/**`, `README.md`, etc.) and exports a `chore` boolean output.
3. Gate every heavy step in the `build` job behind
   `if: needs.changes.outputs.chore != 'true'` so the job still reports
   SUCCESS on chore PRs but does no real work.

This matches `CI.yml`'s structure exactly — `lint` and `tests` already
report SUCCESS as no-ops on chore PRs — so the four required checks
(`changes`, `lint`, `tests`, `build`) behave consistently.

## Relevant files

- `.github/workflows/docs-build.yml` — refactor target.
- `.github/workflows/CI.yml` — reference pattern (do not edit, just mirror).
- `tests/test_docs_build_workflow.py` — adherence test; the assertions
  on trigger paths and on `continue-on-error` may need adjustment to
  reflect the new shape (paths filter moves from workflow trigger to
  `changes` job input).

## Actions

1. Branch off `main`.
2. Refactor `.github/workflows/docs-build.yml`:
   - Trigger: `pull_request:` (no paths), `push: { branches: [main] }`, `workflow_dispatch:`.
   - Add `changes` job at top with `dorny/paths-filter@v3`, outputs `chore`.
   - `build` job: `needs: changes`, `if: ${{ !cancelled() }}`. Every existing step gets `if: needs.changes.outputs.chore != 'true'`.
3. Update `tests/test_docs_build_workflow.py` — re-aim the `required` set: it should now assert the `changes` job exists, the `build` job depends on it, the build step gating uses the chore flag.
4. Run `make check-fast` — must pass.
5. Optional but recommended: trigger one `workflow_dispatch` on main after merge to confirm the refactored workflow still produces a green build PDF artifact.

## Test (first failing)

`tests/test_docs_build_workflow.py::test_docs_build_runs_on_all_pull_requests` —
assert that the loaded YAML has `on.pull_request` set to a dict WITHOUT a `paths`
key (i.e., runs on every PR). Currently the file has `paths: [...]` → red.
After refactor → green.

## Verification

- [ ] `docs-build / build` reports SUCCESS on a STATE-only PR (e.g. PR #638 after rebase).
- [ ] `docs-build / build` reports SUCCESS on a build-input PR and *actually* builds the PDFs (the existing functionality is preserved).
- [ ] `make check` green.
- [ ] Adherence test reflects the new structure.

## Invariants

- The existing build steps (report, slides with `continue-on-error: true`, manuscript, `make check`, artifact uploads) still run on PRs that touch build paths.
- Tectonic + pandoc setup steps still run on those PRs.
- Cache key strategy unchanged.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `.github/workflows/docs-build.yml` refactored to mirror `CI.yml`'s changes-job pattern.
- [ ] Adherence test passes against the new shape.
- [ ] On a chore PR (no build paths touched), `build` reports SUCCESS as a no-op.
- [ ] On a build-paths PR, `build` runs full pipeline.

## Out of scope

- Removing `continue-on-error: true` from the slides step. That follow-on is gated on having a stable green slides baseline, which now exists (0367 landed) — but the explicit ticket for that flip is still pending and not in 0371's scope.
- Changing the trigger paths content beyond removing them from `pull_request.paths` (the path list lives in `changes` job's filter now, same content).

## Related

- Blocker-of: 0358 (cannot flip `build` to required on `main` until this lands; orchestrator must defer the `gh api` branch-protection PATCH until 0371 is merged and a chore PR has demonstrated `build` reporting SUCCESS).
